+# Automatic turn signals
+
+**Menu:** Driving \> Steering \> Lane Change (Auto Turn)
+
+---
+
+<!-- CARROT:SETTING:BEGIN AutoBlinkerControl -->
+<a id="AutoBlinkerControl"></a>
+
+## Automatic turn signals
+
+`AutoBlinkerControl`
+
+0: Off (Bluetooth one-touch remains). 1: Hold Bluetooth signals started at or below 5 km/h until the turn completes; indicate from the ATC audioTurn cue until turn desire ends. 2: Also indicate during actual ATC lane changes, excluding waiting. Same direction cancels a hold; opposite direction switches. Stock lever has priority. Requires a supported Jetson USB-CAN/B1 vehicle.
+
+<!-- CARROT:AUTO:BEGIN AutoBlinkerControl -->
+<!-- CARROT:AUTO:SOURCE facts="73eacbd6d52283f0bc1e927a02aafdd8f675417912f83189f06043a23b892684" semantic="77adaaf68f20d161145a88a9210dfc2c04aa66e0724cebb3a54bac23063fcbd4" review="needs_review" -->
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN OVERVIEW -->
+- **Type:** Segmented choice
+- **Default:** `0`
+- **Range:** `0` ~ `2`
+- **Step:** `1`
+- **Menu:** Driving \> Steering \> Lane Change (Auto Turn)
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END OVERVIEW -->
+<!-- CARROT:AUTO:END AutoBlinkerControl -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:MANUAL:BEGIN AutoBlinkerControl -->
+<!-- CARROT:REVIEW reviewed-for="77adaaf68f20d161145a88a9210dfc2c04aa66e0724cebb3a54bac23063fcbd4" reviewed-at="2026-10-26T00:00:00Z" -->
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+Controls physical lamps on supported Jetson USB-CAN/B1 vehicles. Operating the stock lever ends the owned request.
+
+- **0:** Disables automatic control; Bluetooth one-touch remains available.
+- **1:** Holds signals started by Bluetooth at or below 5 km/h until turn completion, and indicates from the ATC audioTurn cue until turn desire ends.
+- **2:** Also indicates from actual ATC lane-change start through completion. Waiting does not activate the lamps.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+Map remote buttons to Turn on left/right indicator. During a hold, the same button cancels and the opposite button switches direction.
+
+Check illumination and cancellation while parked first. Basic one-touch remains available while driving; this setting does not change steering or lane-change admission.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+Bluetooth turn completion requires steering at least 30 degrees toward the selected turn, then returning within 10 degrees for 0.4 seconds while moving. Departure alone does not cancel; the maximum hold is five minutes.
+
+USB-CAN requests the initial blink; the existing vehicle indicator-hold function maintains it. Input, vehicle-state or communication loss expires the hold request. A hold request is cancelled if initial illumination is not confirmed within four seconds. A rapid opposite input waits for the current OEM sequence to end, keeping only the latest request for at most 3.2 seconds. Cancelling a hold may still allow the remaining OEM flashes to finish. Existing lane-change settings may react to the actual lamp input.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:MANUAL:END AutoBlinkerControl -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SETTING:END AutoBlinkerControl -->
